  "policies": {
    "Betrug": "Own original successful HAND draw of a minion. Capture full original event-time current hand-minion material, then ordinary attributed stored-copy summon. Rush and any-turn-end captured destruction trigger are installed before first entry notification, no battlecry. Hand original remains unchanged.",
    "Tak": "Each actual random insertion member with a known semantic actor equal to recipient/observer player. Use original insertion event and matching DeckShuffleRecord marker, capture event-time full current physical deck-card material and ordinary hand copy. Same semantic operation may insert multiple physical cards and each separately copies once.",
    "FrozenContext": "Existing original event-time RuleContext snapshots and immutable copy material preserve the accepted original source despite prior reactions moving, playing, changing or removing its later physical carrier. Do not reconstruct from current deck search.",
    "EntryGrant": "Existing CreatedMinionGrant gains only finite Rush plus named turn-end destruction for original current HAND stored-copy board delivery. Ordinary active trigger/DestroyCapturedMinion and attachment copy/silence/return/transform/respawn lifecycle remain shared. No new Effect, payload, scheduler or GameState type."
  },
  "uncertainties": [
    "Betrug currently observes successful hand minion draws, following existing Dorian policy. Burned draws, native dormant entry and precise draw-transformation/notification boundaries remain explicit local policies pending CN calibration.",
    "The extra Rush/end-destruction material is installed before every actual copied delivery notification. At any natural turn end an active accepted carrier is destroyed through its original continuous minion reference; silence/return/transform clear the ordinary grant, current copies retain it and fresh Reborn/base copies do not.",
    "Tak uses the actual semantic shuffle actor, recipient and per-entry random insertion marker. Known opponent shuffles and positional placements do not trigger. Unknown issuer into the observed own deck is an explicit unsupported error, never inferred from source owner/controller or silently ignored.",
    "Equal physical entries in a synchronous semantic shuffle operation each produce their own event-time current hand copy. Frozen original copy material and ordinary current-material rules are reused; exact official reactions/control/notification timing remains deferred.",
    "Original twelve-root frontier and the remaining Godfrey/Teron roots stay in scope. Full past source, all other special pools, standard eligibility and version/hotfix/CN alignment remain open."
  ]
